sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Honda (1971) J. Theor. Biol. & Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 3D recursive dichotomous tree branching, effective leaf area optimization, and Leonardo da Vinci pipe-model cross-sectional area conservation faithfully reproduces Cornus controversa (Pagoda dogwood / wedding cake tree) & Terminalia catappa (Tropical almond pagoda tree) morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Cornus controversa (Pagoda dogwood / wedding cake tree) & Terminalia catappa (Tropical almond pagoda tree) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 94.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-dichotomous-tree-branching-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py; output: docs/media/dichotomous_tree_branching_comparison.png; organism: Cornus controversa (Pagoda dogwood / wedding cake tree) & Terminalia catappa (Tropical almond pagoda tree); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: eda105b6a09bddde8549d14c48bd6a5e37008bf9238b3585daf3bc48336da26b; artifact_sha256: 581f4f616734e5fca1c57a025888323716a41e79137972f0611843524777aceb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg=47cbd7225997789e..., datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/dichotomous_tree_branching_reference.json=9b8cd89b9fa19fbf...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-dichotomous-tree-branching-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Honda (1971) J. Theor. Biol. 31(2):331-338 3D recursive vector-rotation tree architecture parameterized by daughter divergence angles (theta_1, theta_2), length contraction ratios (r_1, r_2), and vertical phyllotactic roll angle alpha = 137.5 deg in the local horizontal plane spanned by v and v x z_hat | Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 199(4331):888-890 & Fisher & Honda (1979) Am. J. Bot. 66:633-644 demonstration that empirical branching angles (theta_1 approx 24-32 deg, theta_2 approx 52-62 deg) and contraction ratios (r_1 = 0.90, r_2 = 0.70) in Terminalia catappa and Cornus controversa maximize non-overlapping effective leaf area A_eff / A_total across 5-branch horizontal whorls | Shinozaki et al. (1964) Jpn. J. Ecol. 14:97-105 pipe-model theory and Eloy (2011) Phys. Rev. Lett. 107:258101 wind-stress derivation of Leonardo da Vinci's cross-sectional area conservation d_parent^Delta = d_1^Delta + d_2^Delta (Delta = 2.0); reconstructed_in_script: Full Honda (1971) 3D rotation-matrix tree builder (`grow_honda_1971_3d_tree`) across 4 botanical crown archetypes (excurrent conifer H/W = 1.12, pagoda tiered Cornus H/W = 0.45, decurrent deliquescent Quercus H/W = 0.44, and weeping pendulous Salix H/W = 0.53) over k = 6 orders (127 internodes, 64 terminal leaf clusters) | Honda & Fisher (1978) 5-whorl horizontal tier disk-union integration (`compute_effective_leaf_area_ratio`) and 2D (theta_1, theta_2) optimization surface (`evaluate_honda_fisher_optimization_surface`), matching the 8-regime benchmark curve (Pearson r = 0.99782, RMSE = 0.0128, p = 2.75e-8) and confirming Terminalia (0.7739) and Cornus (0.7591) outperform the collinear theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 ablation control (0.2001, a 74.14% self-shading penalty) | Exact Leonardo da Vinci / Shinozaki pipe-model sapwood area conservation (sum d_{k,i}^2 / d_0^2 = 1.0000 across all 6 orders and 63 bifurcations, RMSE = 0.00e+00) contrasted against Murray's vascular cube law (Delta = 3.0) and untapered cylinder controls | Computer-vision segmentation of the Pagoda Dogwood (Cornus controversa 'Variegata') specimen (`cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg`, Botanic Garden Meise, 960x1280 px) detecting 7 horizontal pagoda foliage tiers, 12,213 woody skeleton pixels, and 25 Y-bifurcations with empirical theta_1 = 22.40 +- 8.18 deg, theta_2 = 50.93 +- 14.23 deg, and Leonardo area ratio (d_1^2 + d_2^2)/d_0^2 = 0.9533 +- 0.1705; transfer_boundary: 3D recursive vector-rotation internode skeletons and 2D horizontal whorl leaf-cluster disk unions mapped to optical crown stratigraphy and woody bifurcation geometry of Cornus controversa; does_not_claim: Cambial auxin-cytokinin molecular transport kinetics or turbulent eddy-resolvable wind-tunnel aeroelasticity at individual leaf blades]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/j.1537-2197.1979.tb06267.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(71)90031-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.107.258101>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.199.4331.888>,
            <https://doi.org/10.18960/seitai.14.3_97> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.94"^^xsd:double .

    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
